# The Piper PA-28-180 Cherokee's checklists, written in this project's own
# words from its Owner's Handbook for the Cherokee "E", section III,
# Operating Instructions, pages 17 to 23 - the handbook docs/ASSETS.md
# already records for this aeroplane's published figures, and which was read
# to write these.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The handbook is in miles an hour and the simulation is in knots.** Every
# speed below is the handbook's figure converted, and the handbook's own
# number is given beside it: 85 mph is 73.9 knots, 100 mph is 86.9, 115 mph
# is 99.9, 50 to 60 mph is 43.4 to 52.1. A band is opened a knot at each end,
# because the handbook's speeds are indicated and the simulation reads
# calibrated.
#
# Only the approach has a numbered checklist in the handbook; the rest of
# section III is written as prose, and these items follow what it says to do,
# in the order it says to do it.
#
# The flight model has no electric fuel pump, no carburettor heat, no
# magneto switch and no parking brake, so the handbook's items for those are
# the pilot's to confirm. Its undercarriage is fixed and its propeller
# fixed-pitch.

phase before-start
confirm Parking brake on, and the carburettor heat full cold
confirm Fuel selector on the tank wanted, and the electric fuel pump on
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle open about a quarter of an inch
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
confirm Master switch on, and the starter engaged by the magneto switch

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running, and the throttle advanced to a taxi setting
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi slowly, with as little brake as will do
confirm Brakes checked as she first moves
confirm The taxiway ahead and the wind both allowed for

phase take-off
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Tab set slightly aft of neutral, for the loading
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 25.5 Flaps up, or twenty-five degrees off a short or soft field
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Full throttle
check velocities/vc-kts >= 42.0 Let her accelerate to 43 to 52 knots (50 to 60 mph)
confirm Ease back only enough to let her fly herself off, no more

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Full throttle for the climb
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
range velocities/vc-kts 63.0 88.0 Climb at 73.9 knots for best rate, or 86.9 en route
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Mixture rich
confirm The nose lowered a little to let her accelerate to the climb speed

phase cruise
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.5 0.95 Power set for the cruise wanted
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm <= 0.95 Mixture leaned for the altitude
confirm Trimmed to hold the height, and the power table consulted

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.1 0.7 Power back for the descent
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Mixture enriched as she comes down
confirm Carburettor heat only if there is a sign of carburettor icing
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure

phase approach
confirm Fuel on the proper tank, and the electric fuel pump on
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture set rich
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 40.5 Flaps set, and not above 99.9 knots (115 mph)
confirm Seat belts fastened
range velocities/vc-kts 63.0 76.0 Trimmed to about 73.9 knots (85 mph) with the flaps up, less three mph a notch

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 25.0 40.5 Full flap for a short and slow landing
range velocities/vc-kts 52.0 70.0 Airspeed reduced through the flare, to contact near the stall
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.3 Enough power to hold the path, and then closed
confirm Hold the nose wheel off as long as it will stay off

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps retracted before the brakes are used
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Slowed, with back pressure holding her on the main wheels
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back for the taxi
confirm Electric fuel pump off, at the pilot's discretion
